<article class="env-lemma" id="0BMN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BMN">Lemma <span data-tag="0BMN">35.13.8</span>.</a> Consider schemes $X, Y, Z$ and morphisms $a, b : X \to Y$ and a morphism $c : Y \to Z$ with $c \circ a = c \circ b$. Set $d = c \circ a = c \circ b$. If there exists an fpqc covering $\{ Z_ i \to Z\} $ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for all $i$ the morphism $Y \times _{c, Z} Z_ i \to Z_ i$ is the coequalizer of $(a, 1) : X \times _{d, Z} Z_ i \to Y \times _{c, Z} Z_ i$ and $(b, 1) : X \times _{d, Z} Z_ i \to Y \times _{c, Z} Z_ i$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $i$ and $i'$ the morphism $Y \times _{c, Z} (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'}) \to (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'})$ is the coequalizer of $(a, 1) : X \times _{d, Z} (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'}) \to Y \times _{c, Z} (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'})$ and $(b, 1) : X \times _{d, Z} (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'}) \to Y \times _{c, Z} (Z_ i \times _ Z Z_{i'})$ 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $c$ is the coequalizer of $a$ and $b$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, for a scheme $T$ a morphism $Z \to T$ is the same thing as a collection of morphism $Z_ i \to T$ which agree on overlaps by Lemma <a href="/tag/023Q" data-tag="023Q">35.13.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>